# eu-u9xj.6 (PP) — a par-map whose f returns a non-serialisable value (a
# function) is a programmer error at the parallel boundary (spec §6). The
# boundary check fires on both the parallel and the sequential paths (both
# round-trip results through the serialisation codec), naming the value kind
# and the combinator.
mkfn(x): (+ x)
result: [1, 2, 3] par-map(mkfn)
